paragraph('We partition the model-implied variance',r'''The decomposition separates variation associated with the measured information from a residual teacher component and variation remaining between decisions. To avoid making the allocation depend on which information is entered first, we average the contribution of each measured block across orders of entry \citep{groemping}. A linear mixed model supplies the main partition, with bootstrap standard errors; logistic specifications check sensitivity to the binary-response model. Appendix~\ref{app:prediction} gives the construction. This analysis describes the fitted structure of decisions, complementing the separate prediction of harshness in held-out teachers.''')
